  "question": {
    "text": "<p>The increasing order of the <math><mi>p</mi><mi>K</mi><mi>a</mi></math> values of the following compounds is:<br /><img src=\"assets\\qt0310_4eb2367903a9.png\" style=\"width: 391px; height: 204px;\" /></p>"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math><mi>B</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>D</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mi>D</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>B</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mi>B</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>D</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>A</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mi>C</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>D</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "A"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>pKa</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mi>logKa</mi></math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Ka</mi><mo>&#8593;</mo><mi>pKa</mi><mo>&#8595;</mo></math>&nbsp;&amp; vice versa<br /><br />Acidic character&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#945;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi>Ka</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#945;</mi><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>pKa</mi></mfrac></math><br /><br />Acidic character &alpha; stability of anion (Conjugate base)<br /><br />Conjugate base are<br /><img src=\"assets\\st0310_7caeb5fc6990.png\" style=\"width: 457px; height: 272px;\" /><br /><br />Stability of conjugate base&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#945;</mi><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>or</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi></math>&nbsp;<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#945;</mi><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>or</mi><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi></mrow></mfrac></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi></math>&nbsp;is more dominating than&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi></math><br /><br /><math> <mrow> <mrow><mo>(</mo> <mi>B</mi> <mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow> </math>&nbsp; &nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8722;</mo><msub><mi>NO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;at para so exerts&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi></math>&nbsp;or&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi></math>&nbsp; &amp; &nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi></math>&nbsp;<mi>&gt;<mi>&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi></math><br /><br />So it is highly stable anion in<br /><br /><math> <mrow> <mrow><mo>(</mo> <mi>C</mi> <mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow> </math>&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>NO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;at meta exerts only&nbsp; <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi></math>&nbsp;effect<br /><br /><math> <mrow> <mrow><mo>(</mo> <mi>A</mi> <mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow> </math>&nbsp;No <math><msup><mrow><mi>e</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo></mrow></msup></math>&nbsp;withdrawing or electron releasing group.<br /><br /><math> <mrow> <mrow><mo>(</mo> <mi>D</mi> <mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow> </math>&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>OCH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;has&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mo>&#38;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi></math>&nbsp;but&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi></math>&nbsp;dominates<br /><br />So acidic strength will be<br /><br /><math><mi>B</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mi>D</mi></math> </mi></mi><br /><br />Therefore <math> <mrow> <mi>p</mi><mi>K</mi><mi>a</mi> </mrow> </math> values will be in the order<br /><br /><math> <mrow> <mi>B</mi><mo>&#60;</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>&#60;</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>&#60;</mo><mi>D</mi> </mrow> </math></p>"
  }
}